<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marie Louise, Duchess of Parma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1791–1847</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Marie Louise of Austria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marie Louise was an Austrian archduchess, daughter of Emperor Francis I, who married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> in 1810 and bore his son, Napoleon II. After Napoleon's fall the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a> gave her the Duchy of Parma, Piacenza and Guastalla for life. She ruled it until her death in 1847, after which Parma passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbons</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marie-louise-duchess-of-parma.jpg" alt="Marie Louise, Duchess of Parma" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean-Baptiste Paulin Guérin / After François Gérard · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Empress_Marie_Louise_of_the_French.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
